    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d14">

                <pb facs="0040" n="18" xml:id="pg18"/>

                <head>14. Letter From President Kennedy to Chairman Khrushchev<anchor n="0" xml:id="d14-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content" calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1962-05-06">undated</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Chairman</hi>: The American people and I
                    sincerely thank you for your<anchor n="1" xml:id="d14-f2"/> message conveying
                    congratulations on behalf of yourself and the Soviet people on the occasion of
                    the flight of Commander Shepard in the first American manned exploration of
                        space.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d14-f3"/></p>
                <p>We believe that the peaceful exploration of space is a venture undertaken on
                    behalf of mankind as a whole. In that spirit, each new step in the conquest and
                    understanding of space, wherever made, will be an achievement in which all of us
                    share.</p>
                <p>Sincerely,<anchor n="3" xml:id="d14-f4"/></p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
